{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera","id":1494183,"title":"Types of Nocnitsa (Chimera)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-02T22:50:14-07:00","id":1494183,"title":"Types of Nocnitsa (Chimera)","content":"I need to brainstorm additional kinds of the Nocnitsa, a type of Orphan Chimera. Per the 2e corebook, Nocnitsa are chimera born from the darkest of nightmares, perhaps the most feared chimera of all. The only example we are given are the Creeping Fear - monstrous spiders.<br /> <br /> It's a great concept, but it is undeveloped. I don't run Changeling games, but I am currently in a Werewolf game with a pack of stag that wants to be heavily involved with the fae. So the idea that Garou packs of Stag defend the fae from Nocnitsa seems an obvious one. I just need something else other than giant spiders or similar vermin.<br /> <br /> It is an easy temptation to just go high fantasy and begin pulling in the equivalent of D&amp;D monsters. But I want to keep close to folklore or thematically appropriate creatures. I also want to avoid creatures that are best interpreted as &quot;monsters under the bed&quot; for children - those are better classified as a kind of Nervosa, as their intent is to scare irrational children, not actually kill them. I see Nocnitsa as far more malevolent or deadly. Nocnitsa are also similar to &quot;Monsters&quot;, but Monsters appear to be a default category of anything else that does fit the categories of Nervosa, Nocnitsa, and Sprites. Monsters might be dangerous, but aren't necessarily malevolent or murderous in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I decided to add the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nachtkrapp\" target=\"_blank\">Nachtkrapps</a> as a kind of Nocnitsa. It's a giant, monstrous raven that flies at night. It could also be a Nervosa, but stories of it killing and devouring children upgrade it in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I also use <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloody_Bones\" target=\"_blank\">Tommy Rawhead</a>, also known as Bloody Bones or Rawhead-and-Bloody Bones. Again while this could also be a Nervosa, its murderous nature makes it better as a Nocnitsa.<br /> <br /> I also think the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Doctors\" target=\"_blank\">Night Doctors</a> would make a good type.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aufhocker\" target=\"_blank\">Aufhockers</a> are also a good possibility since they crush their victims to death.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the creepypasta example of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black-eyed_children\" target=\"_blank\">Black Eyed Kids</a> don't seem to actually murder people, just terrify them. So I'd make them Nervosa instead.<br /> <br /> I am interested in whether people have created or seen used other examples of Nocnitsa in their games. I want to add them to my list as possible chimerical antagonists that Changelines or Garou could fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T04:27:36-07:00","id":1494201,"title":"","content":"Freddy Krueger, at least as presented in the first two films when he was still a serious villain and not a pop culture icon. Not sure what you would call a generic version of that.<br /> <br /> The Greys, the aliens described from certain UFO abduction/night terror stories where one is being subjected to bizarre medical experiments while conscious but unable to move. However, those may fall more under Nervosa. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T11:04:35-07:00","id":1494237,"title":"","content":"Look up online documentation of the hallucinations suffered by people who endure sleep paralysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T22:51:21-07:00","id":1494285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera?p=1494201#post1494201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freddy Krueger, at least as presented in the first two films when he was still a serious villain and not a pop culture icon. Not sure what you would call a generic version of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always mapped Freedy Krueger to a Spectre who has Phantasm and Shroud Rending (plus plenty of other Arcanoi). I'm not sure if a &quot;dream killer&quot; like him should really be a Chimera.<br /> <br /> However, one of my game projects is working on what kinds of encounters and scenarios can be done in Chimares because plenty of splats have powers that involve entering somebody's dreams, but none of the games do a good job of giving STs tools to do that. I like the idea that there can be actual conflicts in someone's dreams as a result of Garou, Wraiths, various Spirits/Banes, and Fae entering them (plus Mages, Vampires with Astral Projection and who knows what else).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera?p=1494201#post1494201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Greys, the aliens described from certain UFO abduction/night terror stories where one is being subjected to bizarre medical experiments while conscious but unable to move. However, those may fall more under Nervosa. \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Greys definitely fit the setting since so much UFO abduction lore mirrors fairy abduction lore. I think it'd be a good kind of Chimera, but probably one of the &quot;Monsters&quot; than a Nocnitsa. It really depends on how the ST portrays them in the setting consistently. The only thing I would be leer on is that since the Greys are so heavily identified in a science fiction setting, that some players might find their presence in Changeling very jarring.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T22:55:40-07:00","id":1494286,"title":"","content":"I also think there's a lot of inspiration that can be taken from the Dreamlands setting of HP Lovecraft/Call of Cthulhu. Creatures like Gugs, Ghasts, and Moonbeasts would probably all qualify as Nocnitsa, though as an ST I would make sure they would only be found in some distant corner of the Dreaming and never in the Autumn World. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't have them be &quot;natural&quot; creatures of the Near Dreaming, but occasional raids from the Deep Dreaming might reach into the Near Dreaming. I'd make it clear that these intruders are from distant realm, some other Dreaming. Not truly alien, but elsewhere (and perhaps tied to exiled Fomorians).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T07:10:30-07:00","id":1494311,"title":"","content":"In the case of Kruger, I was thinking more along the lines of him as inspiration for a more general type of &quot;killer boogieman&quot; figure that adapts to whatever the local kids/teens tell each other, or the local adults' unvoiced fears/guilt might be. Also like the entity in New Nightmare that wears the Kruger identity as its form of choice.<br /> <br /> Personally, I was always disappointed that Changeling didn't incorporate more UFO lore, especially given how big The X Files and the like was in the 90s. A Hunters Hunted type group of former enchanted and ravaging victims who all believe they are alien abduction survivors and the fey are alien invaders would have been interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T10:22:38-07:00","id":1494333,"title":"","content":"There are some interesting fan supplements about sci-if dreams which include UFO lore out now, including one from the \u2018Walking Away From Arcadia\u2019 folk iirc<br /> <br /> Some ideas for Nightmares that might be good:<br /> <br /> \u2022Evil Cars: you could give it a pseudo-personality like Christine or just have it be the chemical form of a car which is looking to hit people and get them into wrecks. Given the amount of nervous energy, horror, and trauma which can surround cars I think they\u2019d be a good fit.<br /> <br /> \u2022Creepy Crawlies: a classic Fomorian image in the same vein of the spiders. Shadowy threats like Giant Spiders, Snakes, Big Cats, Wolves, Mean Dogs (Kujo); all seem like a classic sort of thing which would pop up as potential Nocnitsa<br /> <br /> Thinking about this actually gave me an idea. It might also be useful to look at the setting that your using to draw inspiration for Nocnitsa. If their are cases of animal maulings you get Big Dog Nocnitsa, if people keep dying in wrecks you get Killer Kar Nocnitsa, if a family dies in a house fire you get Hellflame Nocnitsa; etc. The source for these chimera then would be from the dreams (or, nightmares, rather) caused by the experience of lethal trauma and the psychic damage caused by knowing that such terrible threats exist in the world and could strike again at any time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T19:48:00-07:00","id":1494375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera?p=1494333#post1494333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If their are cases of animal maulings you get Big Dog Nocnitsa, if people keep dying in wrecks you get Killer Kar Nocnitsa, if a family dies in a house fire you get Hellflame Nocnitsa; etc. The source for these chimera then would be from the dreams (or, nightmares, rather) caused by the experience of lethal trauma and the psychic damage caused by knowing that such terrible threats exist in the world and could strike again at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea, but I'd likely classify them as Nervosa in my own games since they sound like Chimera that spawned from the minds of people. I imagine Nocnitsa are chimerical inhabitants of the Dreaming itself, though many should be able to enter the Autumn World as well. I imagine Nervosa are primarily in the Autumn World and are not &quot;native&quot; to the Near Dreaming, mostly incidental.<br /> <br /> But the difference between Nervosa, Nocnitsa, and Monsters can sometimes be arbitrary and very much to an individual ST's tastes. Since those categories only exist for the STs benefit, I wouldn't argue about it much. Just argue a little bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-04T20:04:32-07:00","id":1494379,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s all good! I get your point with the thread though, it is tricky to imagine what sort of things spawn from the Dreaming side rather then the Autumn side. Kinda makes me imagine that the Dreaming is getting geological layers made from dream stuff and that these chimera are spawning from said dream-sediment, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> In that sense, something more abstract makes sense to me. Something that represents Terror-unto-Death in an almost Platonic or Jungian way rather then being a symbolic representation of some person(s) fears. <br /> <br /> The first ideas I have are somewhat impressionistic. A darkness that really is malevolent and wants to hurt you. A Beast that wants to chase you down and kill you. A Powerful Thing which towers over you and smashes you. A Vast Thing which swallows and collapses over you. A Crawly Thing which infests you. <br /> <br /> Things which only have sensible forms when they appear before someone whose mind has to contextualize them SOMEHOW and whose brain\u2019s will short circuit to the nearest acceptable representation of what the thing actually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T05:26:31-07:00","id":1494405,"title":"","content":"Oh, FUN!<br /> <br /> For my own tastes and for my games, I have a great deal of overlap between Banes and Nocnitsa. Below is a small bestiary that are in the background of my games. The Svartalves are basically Scrag banes, and serve as shock troops for House Balor and the Thallain (and are a handfull for Changeling characters).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gooshy Gooze (Nocnitsa/Corrupted Toy)</b><br /> Gooshy Gooze is guaranteed to be a million laughs. It swishes, it sloshes, it oozes and it goozes. It also forces itself down the throats of unsuspecting children when they\u2019re left alone at night. Gooshy Gooze is another wonderful \u201cnon-toxic\u201d creation of Avalon Toys. Like most of the dangerous toys from Avalon, Gooshy Gooze doesn\u2019t kill, it corrupts. Unlike most of the dangerous toys, this is not a simple fetish; it is a creature with a mind of its own and needs no child to do its work.<br /> Gooshy Gooze devours its prey from the inside, destroying innocence and sanity as it goes. By the time Gooshy Gooze has finished its consumption, it has transmogrified the hapless child into an equivalent volume of Gooshy Gooze. Most of the Gooshy Gooze then oozes its way back to any of 200 factories nationwide; it is subsequently redistributed to any of Avalon\u2019s countless \u201cbubble gum machines\u201d where it can again be picked up for a measly 25 cents. Many children learn from their friends that these particular machines will sometime even dispense the Gooshy Gooze without a quarter; you just have to turn the knob, and as often as not, the Gooshy Gooze is yours.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Strength 3, Dexterity 2, Stamina 0 (in host body 4), Charisma 0 (in host body 3), Manipulation 0 (in host body 3), Appearance 0 (in host body 2), Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 1<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Athletics 3, Brawl 3, Survival 2<br /> Glamour: 5 Willpower: 5<br /> <b>Health Levels: </b>OK, -2, Incapacitated (can only be hurt by fire, electricity or freezing)<br /> <b>Redes: </b>Possession, Transformation, Wyrd.<br /> <b>Banes:</b> Token (Must use the material Gooshy Gooze to use Wyrd)<ul><li><b>Transformation:</b> Gooshy Goozes force themselves down their victims\u2019 throats (Strength + Athletics vs. Dexterity + Dodge; three successes required). While within a host\u2019s body it slowly transforms its host into the same substance they are made of, and while the process is occurring, are capable of anything that the child is physically capable of: knifing Grandma, burning down the house, the usual stuff. The transformation is extremely slow, depleting one Health Level a day from the host until the victim is Incapacitated, at which time the change is complete. This transformation costs one of the Gooshy Gooze's Glamour per day. While in this \u201cbreeding stage\u201d the effective Health Levels of the Gooze are the same as those of its host (three to four for a small child).</li> </ul>---<br /> <b>Meat Puppet (Nocnitsa/Bane)</b><br /> These spirits embody innocence defiled. Meat Puppets wander the Dreaming in search of those young beings (both human and animal) who have suffered wrongful deaths. A Meat Puppet will possess anything from a drowned kitten to a young child beaten to death by her father. Puppets hunger for the feel of young flesh. They wish only to possess a body and wreak vengeance on those with \u201cnatural\u201d bodies. However, they are not strong enough to take a living body, so they prey upon the dead. They possess the recently dead cadavers of young children or animals.<br /> Although individual Meat Puppets are not very strong, they often appear in groups. Since their bodies have already died, Meat Puppets attack unrelentingly and can only be stopped by utterly destroying the host body. Thus, even a group of Meat Puppet \u201ckittens\u201d can be very dangerous.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Strength 1 (3 in host), Dexterity 3 (3 in host), Stamina 1 (3 in host)<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Brawl 1, Survival 2<br /> Glamour: 4, Willpower: 5<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> (in Chimera form) OK, -2, -5, Incapacitated (In Host) OK, OK, OK, OK, OK, OK, Destroyed<br /> <b>Redes: </b>Animate Dead, Traverse Dreaming, Wyrd.<ul><li><b>Animate Dead: </b>The chimera can take over a dead body of a creature of the Dreaming and send it against the living. Roll Glamour vs local Banality. A zombie thus animated has Physical Attributes of 3 each; 7 no-penalty Health levels and a Brawl of 3 but no other Attributes. It only works with one corpse at a time. Nasty chimera may use any Social Abilities they have through the host body to intimidate, harass, seduce or traumatize living victims. The chimera may use this Rede on corpses of mortals if it also possesses the Wyrd rede.Use Cost: 1 Glamour</li> </ul><b>---<br /> Nocturnae </b><b>(Nocnitsa/Bane)</b><br /> The Nocturna, or Nighthag, is the warper of hopes and dreams. This spirit wanders the Dreaming in search of sleeping humans. When it finds a sleeper whose dreaming mind appeals to the Nocturna, the chimera will attempt to twist the dream down a more sinister course. If the sleeper dreams of prosperity and wealth, the Nocturna may corrupt the dream into a fantasy where the dreamer gains wealth only to lose it from the betrayal of a loved one. Dreams of love may turn into terrifying nightmares in which the dreamer\u2019s lover spurns and mocks him. No matter what the fantasy, a Nocturna will cause the dream to devolve into a depressing, hopeless situation. In her physical form, the Nocturna appears as a terrifyingly beautiful woman with long tangled hair, sharp claws, and a mouth filled with pus.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2, Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 4, Perception 2, Intelligence 3, Wits 4<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Alertness 2, Brawl 3, Empathy 4,<br /> Glamour: 6 Willpower: 5<br /> <b>Health Levels: </b>OK, -1, -1, -2, -2, -5, Incapacitated<br /> <b>Attack:</b> Claw for five dice (lethal).<br /> <b>Redes:</b> Dreamweaving, Enchantment, Weapon (Claws)<ul><li><b>Dreamweaving: </b>This Rede works only on sleeping victims in the mundane world when deployed by chimera in the Dreaming. Characters sleeping in the Dreaming are unaffected. Chimera not in the Dreaming cannot utilize this Rede. To activate Dreamweaving, the chimera merely needs to encounter a sleeping victim and gain at least one success on a Glamour roll (difficulty equals the victim\u2019s Willpower). For the remainder of the scene, the chimera can direct the course of the victim\u2019s dream in any manner she sees fit. Successive Dreamweavings on the same victim become easier over a period of time. For every two Dreamweaving attempts, the victim suffers -1 to his Willpower dice pool to resist. Repeated use of this rede causes the victim to gain no benefits from sleep. Over time, the target suffers permanent loss of Willpower, insanity, and death.<b>Use Cost: </b>This Rede costs no Glamour to use. It is actually a limited form of Ravaging, as the chimera gains Glamour from the victim over a period of time.</li> </ul><b>---<br /> Svartalves</b> (<b>Nocnitsa/Bane)</b><br /> These \u201cdark elves\u201d make up one of the many races of warrior-chimera that serve the Elder Dark. They are monsters of unrestrained rage and violence, serving not as corrupters, but as soldiers. They are, literally, dreams of murder. They live for the moment when a victim\u2019s life ends, and they revel in the mayhem and bloodshed they inflict. Packs of Svarts often indulge in frenzies of death and dismemberment, expressing only a malevolently dark humor at their victim\u2019s expense. Svarts are lanky and bony, with glistening gray-black skin, greasy black hair, and crystal blue eyes. Their movements are reminiscent of spiders or small predatory animals. Their walk in a slouch, their arms nearly acting as forelegs. This slouch does not impede their movement in any way.<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 4, Dexterity 2, Stamina 4, Perception 2, Intelligence 1, Wits 1<br /> <b>Abilities:</b> Alertness 3, Athletics (Climbing) 4, Kenning 2, Brawl 3, Intimidation 3, Stealth 4<br /> Glamour 4, Willpower 6<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> OK, -1, -2, -5, Incapacitated<br /> <b>Attack:</b> Bite for six dice (lethal); claw for five dice (lethal).<br /> <b>Redes:</b> *Corruption, Scuttle, Weapons (claws and fangs), Wyrd<ul><li><b>Corruption: </b>The Svart can inspire frenzy in others. The Svart spends a Willpower point, and anyone in the vicinity must make a Willpower roll (difficulty of the chimeras permanent Glamour), or succumb to the frenzy, indulging in their darkest, nastiest desires. The chimera may use this Rede on mortals if it also possesses the Enchantment or Wyrd redes.</li> </ul>---<br /> <br /> <b>POLLUTION NOCNITSA</b><br /> Pollution Elementals are also favorite Nocnitsa. These are both akin to Inanimae and Plague Nervosa, but are far deadlier. The Near Dreaming adjacent to large cities are thick with these creatures, as are Dream Realms connected to Industry and many Nightmare Realms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hogling (Smog)</b><br /> These appear as roughly humanoid clouds of noxious fumes, ominously rolling toward their targets. As with other elemental chimera of corruption, these Nocnitsa can be found in polluted areas in great numbers. They normally remain inactive unless disturbed, but will prey on Changelings and other beings when the opportunity presents itself.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Strength 5, Dexterity 6, Stamina 2, Perception 3, Intelligence 2, Wits 2<br /> <b>Abilities: </b>Alertness 5, Athletics 4, Kenning 5, Brawl 1, Dodge 6, Stealth 8, Streetwise 6, Gremayre 4<br /> Glamour 7, Willpower 3, Banality 0<br /> <b>Health: </b>OK, -1, -2, -4, Inc<br /> <b>Redes: </b>Befuddle, Enchantment, Fester, Flight, Hide, Poof Begone, Traverse Dreaming.<br /> <br /> <b>H\u2019ruggling (Sludge)</b><img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTy4hGH-fEDBI55mnq5Rjb4COO2xO66VgZijVmUoqzbc-TN2faO\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Also called Monsturds and Stinklings, these gross chimera appear as roughly humanoid piles of waste. They lumber and ooze toward their victims, leaving slimy trails in their wakes. As with other elemental chimera of corruption, these Nocnitsa can be found in polluted areas in great numbers. They normally remain inactive unless disturbed, but will prey on Changelings and other beings when the opportunity presents itself.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Strength 6, Dexterity 2, Stamina 7, Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 1<br /> <b>Abilities: </b>Alertness 4, Brawl 4, Kenning 3, Survival (sewers) 5<br /> Glamour 5, Willpower 9, Banality 0<br /> <b>Health Levels:</b> OK, -1, -2, -4, Inc<br /> <b>Redes:</b> Armor (4), Corruption, Fester, Meld (Corrupted Earth), Venom, Wyrd<br /> <br /> <b>Wakshaani (Toxins)</b><br /> These appear as roughly humanoid blobs of purplish fluid covered with blotches, veins and bubbling wart. As with other elemental chimera of corruption, these Nocnitsa can be found in polluted areas in great numbers. They normally remain inactive unless disturbed, but will prey on Changelings and other beings when the opportunity presents itself.<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Stamina 6, Perception 2, Intelligence 2, Wits 3<br /> <b>Abilities: </b>Athletics (swim) 5, Alertness 3, Brawl 4, Crafts (fishing) 5,Dodge 5, Kenning 4, Stealth 5<br /> Glamour 7, Willpower 3, Banality 0<br /> <b>Health: </b>OK, -1, -2, -4, Inc<br /> <b>Redes: </b>Aggravated Damage (Venom), Corruption, Element Sense, Fester, Traverse Dreaming, Venom, Wyrd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-05-2022, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T12:34:32-07:00","id":1494429,"title":"","content":"I see someone really likes their 1st edition Book of the Wyrm! It does have some great Banes that aren't found elsewhere, and I like the development of Avalon Toys in it which was a company rather neglected in future material (sometimes a bit over the top in my opinion - it strains credibility that Gooshy Gooze is so dangerous, it works best as a very rare monster disguised as a toy, and most Gooshy Gooze sold are harmless except for perhaps some Wyrm taint). Unfortunately later development of Avalon Toys became less about a horror concept of people developing monsters and cursed toys to harm children, and more about leftwing talking points criticizing the actual toy industry.<br /> <br /> I agree that a lot of Banes can be transitioned to Chimera and go back and forth, simply because there's so much overlap in concepts that can be used in both the Penumbra in Werewolf and Chimerical reality in Changeling. The mechanics you use just depends on the game you are playing. I'd definitely have the Nocturnae spirit have a counterpart among or actually be one of the Nocnitsa. It fits perfectly. But I wouldn't use those other Banes as one because they depart too much from my conception of what Nocnitsa should be. But I think it'd be totally fine for Changelings to encounter Fomori or other Wyrm monsters, and you can work those concepts into a Changeling chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 10-05-2022, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T12:45:39-07:00","id":1494430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera?p=1494379#post1494379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first ideas I have are somewhat impressionistic. A darkness that really is malevolent and wants to hurt you. A Beast that wants to chase you down and kill you. A Powerful Thing which towers over you and smashes you. A Vast Thing which swallows and collapses over you. A Crawly Thing which infests you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those are all sound concepts to begin with. The difficulty of course is turning them into something gameable - providing a solid description, giving it a name, and placing it appropriately in the greater setting. But some kind of Engulfing Darkness, or a creature that could swallow you whole in a single gulp are great concepts. <br /> <br /> The primal fears of mankind get at the heart of the Nocnitsa. The fear of the unknown things in the dark, mutilation, crawling creatures, being killed, being helpless and unable to move, being eaten, etc. need to be represented in some manner. And there should be multiple expressions of each same basic fears. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T12:59:45-07:00","id":1494433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera?p=1494429#post1494429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see someone really likes their 1st edition Book of the Wyrm! It does have some great Banes that aren't found elsewhere, and I like the development of Avalon Toys in it which was a company rather neglected in future material (sometimes a bit over the top in my opinion - it strains credibility that Gooshy Gooze is so dangerous, it works best as a very rare monster disguised as a toy, and most Gooshy Gooze sold are harmless except for perhaps some Wyrm taint). Unfortunately later development of Avalon Toys became less about a horror concept of people developing monsters and cursed toys to harm children, and more about leftwing talking points criticizing the actual toy industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well spotted! I love that book. But it can make a game into a b-movie splatterfest very quickly. Avalon is in the backdrop of my games, but I have not used them overtly yet. The Svarts/Scrags are damned dangerous foes for Changeling, where they are fodder for werewolves.<br /> <br /> As for fomori, I use them in Changeling, but they are less powerful sorts. Enticers, toads and similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-05-2022, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T16:20:19-07:00","id":1494631,"title":"","content":"In my games, changelings and all things fae are 100% of the Wyld. I find it a great disservice to the Wyld\u2019s creation-based power to restrict evil to the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T07:42:53-07:00","id":1494729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494183-types-of-nocnitsa-chimera?p=1494631#post1494631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games, changelings and all things fae are 100% of the Wyld. I find it a great disservice to the Wyld\u2019s creation-based power to restrict evil to the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you.<br /> <br /> Personally, it seems to me that the Fomrians were originally of the Wyld or Wyrm of Balance. But their binding at the war of the trees (with the Weavers help) doomed them and the Wyld. Now, most of what was once a mighty force of the Wyld is mostly Wyrm tainted.<br /> <br /> I would even go so far as to say that the Fomrians need to be rescued from their prisons if Gaea is to survive. This would be bad news for civilization as the WOD knows it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-10-2022, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T10:15:22-07:00","id":1494741,"title":"","content":"The Zmei were originally beings of the Wyld that were corrupted by the Wyrm. I imagine that any truly metaphysical evil (as opposed to being an equivalent of Mother Nature is dangerous) in the Dreaming is the same. Originally everything within it was of the Wyld. Most Unseelie, Denizens, Nocnitsa, etc. are not of the Wyrm. But there are certain members who would be considered as such because they've gone too far and would now be considered to be corrupted by the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Coincidentally, I just saw there are more Chimera in the Dreams &amp; Nightmares sourcebook. Although not organized as such in the book, I think certain Chimera there would fall under the Nocnitsa category like the Rakshasha and Morae. And in the description of the Morae, it says that some of them are corrupted by the Wyrm and known as the Nocturnae banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}